# Walkthrough - Bulk Insert Stability & Logging

I have overhauled the bulk medicine insertion process to ensure that all records are saved correctly and any failures are individually logged and skipped without affecting the rest of the batch.

## Changes Made

### 1. Resilient Bulk Insertion
Refactored [app/api/medicines/bulk-insert/route.ts](file:///c:/Users/vaibh/Documents/Ayur-stock%20pro/app/api/medicines/bulk-insert/route.ts):
- **Removed Global Transaction**: Switched from a single `prisma.$transaction` to individual record processing. This prevents one bad record from rolling back all 270+ medicines.
- **Individual Error Handling**: Wrapped every medicine save operation in a `try...catch` block.
- **Improved Finding Logic**: Strengthened the check for existing medicines by matching on `shopId`, `name`, `company`, AND `packing`.

### 2. Comprehensive Logging
Added detailed server-side console logs for every medicine in the batch:
- **`Saved (NEW)`**: Logged when a new medicine record is created.
- **`Saved (UPDATED)`**: Logged when an existing record is updated with new data (HSN, category, etc.).
- **`Skipped (EXISTS)`**: Logged when the medicine already exists and no updates are needed.
- **`FAILED`**: Logged with the specific error message (e.g., unique constraint violation on barcode) for debugging.

## Verification Results

### Automated Tests
- `npm run lint`: Passed.
- `npm run build`: Successfully completed production build.

### Performance & Durability
- The API now returns a summary including `errorCount`, allowing you to see exactly how many records failed if any.
- By removing the global transaction, the system can now handle very large imports (270+ items) without the risk of an all-or-nothing failure.
